  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "atomId": "atom-1",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-1",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "Donald Trump has now been given at least two experimental COVID-19 treatments. ",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 79,
          "context": "Donald Trump has now been given at least two experimental COVID-19 treatments.  Here's what we know about them\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "After being given an experimental antibody cocktail and relocating to a military hospital, US President Donald Trump has now been prescribed the unproven COVID-19 treatment remdesivir.\n",
          "start": 110,
          "end": 295,
          "context": "Here's what we know about them\n After being given an experimental antibody cocktail and relocating to a military hospital, US President Donald Trump has now been prescribed the unproven COVID-19 treatment remdesivir.\n Mr Trump, 74, was moved into a special suite at Walter Reed National Military Medical Centre about 24 hours after testing positive to coronavirus.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-43",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "Early in the pandemic, Mr Trump backed the idea of using anti-malaria drug Hydroxychloroquine to treat COVID-19.\n",
          "start": 5170,
          "end": 5283,
          "context": "How about hydroxychloroquine?\n Early in the pandemic, Mr Trump backed the idea of using anti-malaria drug Hydroxychloroquine to treat COVID-19.\n In May, the President said he was taking the drug to prevent an infection.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-71",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "View original content:http://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/regenerons-regn-cov2-antibody-cocktail-reduced-viral-levels-and-improved-symptoms-in-non-hospitalized-covid-19-patients-301140336.html\n",
          "start": 14234,
          "end": 14431,
          "context": "mark.hudson@regeneron.com\n View original content:http://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/regenerons-regn-cov2-antibody-cocktail-reduced-viral-levels-and-improved-symptoms-in-non-hospitalized-covid-19-patients-301140336.html\n SOURCE"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-11",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "All patients entering the trial had laboratory-confirmed COVID-19 that was being treated in the outpatient setting. ",
          "start": 1302,
          "end": 1418,
          "context": "Patients in the trial were randomized 1:1:1 to receive a one-time infusion of 8 grams of REGN-COV2 (high dose), 2.4 grams of REGN-COV2 (low dose) or placebo.  All patients entering the trial had laboratory-confirmed COVID-19 that was being treated in the outpatient setting.  Patients were prospectively characterized prior to treatment by serology tests to see if they had already generated antiviral antibodies on their own and were classified as seronegative (no measurable antiviral antibodies) or seropositive (measurable antiviral antibodies). "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-8",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "\"After months of incredibly hard work by our talented team, we are extremely gratified to see that Regeneron's antibody cocktail REGN-COV2 rapidly reduced viral load and associated symptoms in infected COVID-19 patients,\" said\n",
          "start": 597,
          "end": 824,
          "context": "This trial is part of a larger program that also includes studies of REGN-COV2 for the treatment of hospitalized patients, and for prevention of infection in people who have been exposed to COVID-19 patients.\n \"After months of incredibly hard work by our talented team, we are extremely gratified to see that Regeneron's antibody cocktail REGN-COV2 rapidly reduced viral load and associated symptoms in infected COVID-19 patients,\" said\n The descriptive analysis included the first 275 patients enrolled in the trial and was designed to evaluate anti-viral activity with REGN-COV2 and identify patients most likely to benefit from treatment; the next cohort, which could be used to rapidly and prospectively confirm these results, has already been enrolled. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-12",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "The technique is already in wide use for treating a range of illnesses.\n",
          "start": 1267,
          "end": 1339,
          "context": "REGN-COV2 — which contains an antibody made by Regeneron and a second isolated from humans who recovered from COVID-19 — is designed so that its two antibodies bind to the coronavirus' spike protein, limiting the ability of viruses to escape.\n The technique is already in wide use for treating a range of illnesses.\n Regeneron said it agreed to supply a single dose, given through an IV, for Mr Trump at the request of his physician under \"compassionate use\" provisions, when an experimental medicine is provided on a case-by-case emergency basis, while studies continue.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-1",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "Donald Trump has now been given at least two experimental COVID-19 treatments. ",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 79,
          "context": "Donald Trump has now been given at least two experimental COVID-19 treatments.  Here's what we know about them\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "This trial is part of a larger program that also includes studies of REGN-COV2 for the treatment of hospitalized patients, and for prevention of infection in people who have been exposed to COVID-19 patients.\n",
          "start": 388,
          "end": 597,
          "context": "Regeneron to host investor and media webcast to discuss results at\n This trial is part of a larger program that also includes studies of REGN-COV2 for the treatment of hospitalized patients, and for prevention of infection in people who have been exposed to COVID-19 patients.\n \"After months of incredibly hard work by our talented team, we are extremely gratified to see that Regeneron's antibody cocktail REGN-COV2 rapidly reduced viral load and associated symptoms in infected COVID-19 patients,\" said\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-54",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "REGN-COV2's development and manufacturing has been funded in part with federal funds from the\n",
          "start": 7805,
          "end": 7899,
          "context": "Preclinical studies have shown that REGN-COV2 reduced the amount of virus and associated damage in the lungs of non-human primates.\n REGN-COV2's development and manufacturing has been funded in part with federal funds from the\n About Regeneron\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-56",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "Regeneron is accelerating and improving the traditional drug development process through our proprietary VelociSuite technologies, such as VelocImmune®, which uses unique genetically-humanized mice to produce optimized fully-human antibodies and bispecific antibodies, and through ambitious research initiatives such as the Regeneron Genetics Center, which is conducting one of the largest genetics sequencing efforts in the world.\n",
          "start": 7915,
          "end": 8347,
          "context": "About Regeneron\n Regeneron is accelerating and improving the traditional drug development process through our proprietary VelociSuite technologies, such as VelocImmune®, which uses unique genetically-humanized mice to produce optimized fully-human antibodies and bispecific antibodies, and through ambitious research initiatives such as the Regeneron Genetics Center, which is conducting one of the largest genetics sequencing efforts in the world.\n For additional information about the company, please visit www.regeneron.com or follow @Regeneron on Twitter.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-28",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "The data also suggested a possible survival benefit.\n",
          "start": 3714,
          "end": 3767,
          "context": "In May, the FDA approved emergency use of remdesivir to treat COVID-19 after preliminary results from the large randomised controlled trial in the US showed patients recovered four days faster with the drug than with a placebo.\n The data also suggested a possible survival benefit.\n Other more recent studies have shown mixed results.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-57",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "For additional information about the company, please visit www.regeneron.com or follow @Regeneron on Twitter.\n",
          "start": 8347,
          "end": 8457,
          "context": "Regeneron is accelerating and improving the traditional drug development process through our proprietary VelociSuite technologies, such as VelocImmune®, which uses unique genetically-humanized mice to produce optimized fully-human antibodies and bispecific antibodies, and through ambitious research initiatives such as the Regeneron Genetics Center, which is conducting one of the largest genetics sequencing efforts in the world.\n For additional information about the company, please visit www.regeneron.com or follow @Regeneron on Twitter.\n Forward-Looking Statements and Use of Digital Media\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-56",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "Regeneron is accelerating and improving the traditional drug development process through our proprietary VelociSuite technologies, such as VelocImmune®, which uses unique genetically-humanized mice to produce optimized fully-human antibodies and bispecific antibodies, and through ambitious research initiatives such as the Regeneron Genetics Center, which is conducting one of the largest genetics sequencing efforts in the world.\n",
          "start": 7915,
          "end": 8347,
          "context": "About Regeneron\n Regeneron is accelerating and improving the traditional drug development process through our proprietary VelociSuite technologies, such as VelocImmune®, which uses unique genetically-humanized mice to produce optimized fully-human antibodies and bispecific antibodies, and through ambitious research initiatives such as the Regeneron Genetics Center, which is conducting one of the largest genetics sequencing efforts in the world.\n For additional information about the company, please visit www.regeneron.com or follow @Regeneron on Twitter.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-19",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "Regeneron this week reported trial results showing its drug improved symptoms in non-hospitalised COVID-19 patients, with no serious side effects, and said it planned to talk with the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) about an emergency use authorisation.\n",
          "start": 2313,
          "end": 2570,
          "context": "Data so far is limited for COVID-19 antibodies, but US infectious disease chief Anthony Fauci is among those saying it has promise.\n Regeneron this week reported trial results showing its drug improved symptoms in non-hospitalised COVID-19 patients, with no serious side effects, and said it planned to talk with the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) about an emergency use authorisation.\n What about remdesivir?\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-765a0e4b3d83::sentence-8",
          "documentId": "doc-765a0e4b3d83",
          "text": "\"After months of incredibly hard work by our talented team, we are extremely gratified to see that Regeneron's antibody cocktail REGN-COV2 rapidly reduced viral load and associated symptoms in infected COVID-19 patients,\" said\n",
          "start": 597,
          "end": 824,
          "context": "This trial is part of a larger program that also includes studies of REGN-COV2 for the treatment of hospitalized patients, and for prevention of infection in people who have been exposed to COVID-19 patients.\n \"After months of incredibly hard work by our talented team, we are extremely gratified to see that Regeneron's antibody cocktail REGN-COV2 rapidly reduced viral load and associated symptoms in infected COVID-19 patients,\" said\n The descriptive analysis included the first 275 patients enrolled in the trial and was designed to evaluate anti-viral activity with REGN-COV2 and identify patients most likely to benefit from treatment; the next cohort, which could be used to rapidly and prospectively confirm these results, has already been enrolled. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-9",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "Regeneron's cocktail, REGN-COV2, is part of a class of experimental COVID-19 treatments known as monoclonal antibodies.\n",
          "start": 792,
          "end": 912,
          "context": "The President's physician, Sean Conley, said in a statement that Mr Trump \"remains fatigued but in good spirits\" after receiving an intravenous dose of Regeneron Pharmaceuticals' dual antibody.\n Regeneron's cocktail, REGN-COV2, is part of a class of experimental COVID-19 treatments known as monoclonal antibodies.\n Antibodies are proteins made by the body's immune system that recognise, bind and neutralise an invading virus.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-cddf1335a5a6::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-cddf1335a5a6",
          "text": "The dual antibody treatment is called REGN-COV2\n",
          "start": 550,
          "end": 598,
          "context": "Here's what we know.\n The dual antibody treatment is called REGN-COV2\n The President's physician, Sean Conley, said in a statement that Mr Trump \"remains fatigued but in good spirits\" after receiving an intravenous dose of Regeneron Pharmaceuticals' dual antibody.\n"
        }
      ]
    }
